Rules:
  [P1] Define performance baselines before testing.
  [P2] Use realistic data and traffic patterns.
  [P3] Test at 2x expected peak load.
  [P4] Monitor system metrics (CPU, memory, network).
  [P5] Test with gradual ramp-up.
  [P6] Use distributed load generators for scale.
  [P7] Analyze bottlenecks before optimization.
  [P8] Document performance regression thresholds.

Pros:
  - Catch performance issues
  - Capacity planning
  - User experience

Cons:
  - Time-consuming
  - Complex setup
  - Cost

Alternatives:
  - Load testing as a service
  - Synthetic monitoring

State: +

